# Accessibility

- Semantic HTML first: landmarks, headings in order, labeled form controls.
- All interactive elements must be keyboard reachable with visible `:focus-visible`.
- Images need meaningful `alt` (or empty alt for decorative).
- Do not rely on color alone for status; pair with text/icon.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` — globals already dampen transitions.
- Target WCAG 2.2 AA contrast on navy/teal/light surfaces.
- Mega-menus and dialogs need Escape, focus trap, and aria attributes when implemented.
